
WEBVTT

00:00:00.539 --> 00:00:02.720
Marcel is a French mouse.

00:00:02.780 --> 00:00:06.484
He lives on a beautiful old boat in Paris.

00:00:06.544 --> 00:00:10.856
His home is under the kitchen floor.

00:00:10.916 --> 00:00:17.420
He likes books, restaurants and old films.

00:00:17.480 --> 00:00:20.703
He likes the opera too.

00:00:20.763 --> 00:00:27.174
One evening in June, Marcel finishes a detective story.

00:00:27.234 --> 00:00:31.351
Then he goes to have dinner with some friends.

00:00:31.412 --> 00:00:35.114
They live in the metro station at the Louvre.

00:00:35.174 --> 00:00:39.536
After dinner, Marcel waits at the station.

00:00:39.596 --> 00:00:43.538
He sees two men standing next to him.

00:00:43.598 --> 00:00:47.390
The tall one is reading a magazine.

00:00:47.450 --> 00:00:50.702
"Look," he says.

00:00:50.762 --> 00:00:52.772
"Here she is.

00:00:52.832 --> 00:00:56.582
Opera star, Miss Zaza Dupont,

00:00:56.642 --> 00:01:31.243
with her beautiful one-million-pound diamond ring, the White Star."
"Her beautiful diamond ring!" The short man looks at the photo and laughs.
"Not after tonight," he says.
Marcel's mouth opens.
What?
He remembers an evening at the opera two weeks before.

00:01:31.303 --> 00:01:38.748
Zaza's green dress, the music, the beautiful White Star on her finger.

00:01:38.808 --> 00:01:44.720
No, they can't steal it!

00:01:44.780 --> 00:01:50.474
The train comes and the men get on.

00:01:50.533 --> 00:01:55.746
Marcel pulls down his hat and follows them.

00:01:55.806 --> 00:02:01.639
Half an hour later, he gets off again at La Muette station.

00:02:01.698 --> 00:02:07.282
But there are hundreds of people, and Marcel loses the two men.

00:02:07.342 --> 00:02:10.646
Then he sees an old mouse.

00:02:10.706 --> 00:02:14.048
"Excuse me," he says.

00:02:14.108 --> 00:02:17.911
"Do you know where Zaza Dupont lives?"

00:02:17.971 --> 00:02:23.406
But when Marcel finds Zaza's house, it's too late.

00:02:23.466 --> 00:02:25.998
"Yes, two men,"

00:02:26.058 --> 00:02:29.150
she's telling the police on the telephone.

00:02:29.210 --> 00:02:32.222
"And they've got the White Star!"

00:02:32.282 --> 00:02:37.896
At that moment, Marcel hears a motor start.

00:02:37.956 --> 00:02:42.739
"Where's that coming from?"

00:02:42.798 --> 00:02:44.270
he thinks.

00:02:44.330 --> 00:02:47.912
Then he sees something at the end of the road.

00:02:47.972 --> 00:02:49.523
It's them!

00:02:49.583 --> 00:02:51.034
It's the thieves!

00:02:51.094 --> 00:02:53.365
And they're stealing a car.

00:02:53.425 --> 00:02:58.206
He runs across Zaza's garden and down the street.

00:02:58.266 --> 00:03:01.258
He can see the car's number plate.

00:03:01.318 --> 00:03:03.099
It's near.

00:03:03.159 --> 00:03:05.090
Very near.

00:03:05.150 --> 00:03:06.850
"Can I?"

00:03:06.910 --> 00:03:08.411
he thinks.

00:03:08.471 --> 00:03:11.212
And he jumps.

00:03:11.272 --> 00:03:13.464
Yes!

00:03:13.523 --> 00:03:16.794
Marcel sits on the number plate.

00:03:16.854 --> 00:03:19.536
"Good," he thinks.

00:03:19.596 --> 00:03:25.937
Then, after a second or two, "What happens now?"

00:03:25.997 --> 00:03:30.300
The thieves drive across Paris very fast.

00:03:30.360 --> 00:03:33.214
Marcel can hear them in the car.

00:03:33.273 --> 00:03:36.056
They're laughing and talking.

00:03:36.116 --> 00:03:38.878
But Marcel is not laughing.

00:03:38.938 --> 00:03:42.631
He is very, very angry.

00:03:42.691 --> 00:03:47.646
After half an hour, the car stops next to a café.

00:03:47.706 --> 00:03:51.229
It's late and the café is quiet.

00:03:51.289 --> 00:03:54.402
In one corner is a woman.

00:03:54.462 --> 00:03:57.254
The thieves sit at her table.

00:03:57.314 --> 00:04:02.148
Marcel sits under the table and listens.

00:04:02.208 --> 00:04:04.630
"Have you got it?"

00:04:04.689 --> 00:04:06.760
the woman asks.

00:04:06.820 --> 00:04:10.344
The tall man takes a box from his jacket.

00:04:10.403 --> 00:04:12.476
Then he opens it.

00:04:12.535 --> 00:04:16.658
"Look," he says.

00:04:16.718 --> 00:04:21.087
The woman puts a hand to her mouth.

00:04:21.147 --> 00:04:24.764
"What a beautiful diamond!"

00:04:24.824 --> 00:04:28.656
"This is it," thinks Marcel.

00:04:28.716 --> 00:04:31.026
"This is the moment."

00:04:31.086 --> 00:04:36.638
He bites the tall man's leg very hard.

00:04:36.698 --> 00:04:41.450
The tall man throws up his arms.

00:04:41.510 --> 00:04:46.522
The box and the White Star fly across the room.

00:04:46.581 --> 00:04:49.632
"What's that on the floor?"

00:04:49.692 --> 00:04:52.043
one waiter asks.

00:04:52.103 --> 00:04:55.575
"I don't know," says another.

00:04:55.635 --> 00:04:57.066
"Is it?

00:04:57.126 --> 00:04:58.697
No.

00:04:58.757 --> 00:05:01.588
It can't be a diamond."

00:05:01.648 --> 00:05:07.783
But before he can finish, Marcel runs across the room.

00:05:07.843 --> 00:05:11.756
He puts the White Star around his neck.

00:05:11.816 --> 00:05:14.888
Then he runs to the door.

00:05:14.948 --> 00:05:18.972
The thieves jump up and follow him.

00:05:19.032 --> 00:05:25.167
Suddenly, there are tables and chairs everywhere.

00:05:25.227 --> 00:05:28.799
"What's happening?"

00:05:28.859 --> 00:05:31.400
an old man asks.

00:05:31.460 --> 00:05:33.452
"I don't know,"

00:05:33.512 --> 00:05:35.653
his wife answers.

00:05:35.712 --> 00:05:40.726
"Who can understand young people these days?"

00:05:40.786 --> 00:05:43.886
"Stop that mouse!"

00:05:43.946 --> 00:05:46.218
says the tall man.

00:05:46.278 --> 00:05:48.636
"Shut the door!"

00:05:48.696 --> 00:05:51.054
says the short one.

00:05:51.114 --> 00:05:53.515
But they're too late.

00:05:53.575 --> 00:05:59.068
Marcel runs out of the café and doesn't look back.

00:05:59.128 --> 00:06:02.620
After ten minutes, he stops.

00:06:02.680 --> 00:06:04.911
There's nobody following him.

00:06:04.971 --> 00:06:08.222
But where is he?

00:06:08.282 --> 00:06:11.984
Marcel looks right and left.

00:06:12.044 --> 00:06:15.886
Then he sees a big white church.

00:06:15.946 --> 00:06:23.636
"Ah, the Sacré-Cœur," he thinks. "Now I know where I am."

00:06:23.696 --> 00:06:31.178
It's late, and there are no metro trains, but Marcel isn't tired.

00:06:31.237 --> 00:06:34.768
He walks back to Zaza's house.

00:06:34.828 --> 00:06:39.170
When he gets there, she's asleep in bed.

00:06:39.230 --> 00:06:42.291
There's a table next to the window.

00:06:42.351 --> 00:06:49.580
On it, Marcel can see lots of photographs, boxes, and perfume bottles.

00:06:49.640 --> 00:06:55.360
He runs across the floor and up one leg of the table.

00:06:55.420 --> 00:06:58.421
"Now," he thinks.

00:06:58.481 --> 00:07:02.073
"It's time to take off the White Star.

00:07:02.133 --> 00:07:06.406
In the morning, Zaza is going to be very..."

00:07:06.465 --> 00:07:09.746
Then Marcel stops.

00:07:09.806 --> 00:07:12.178
"Oh, no!"

00:07:12.238 --> 00:07:15.020
He can't take the ring off.

00:07:15.080 --> 00:07:18.271
He pulls and pulls.

00:07:18.331 --> 00:07:20.518
But nothing happens.

00:07:20.578 --> 00:07:22.166
"Now what?"

00:07:22.225 --> 00:07:23.617
he thinks.

00:07:23.676 --> 00:07:28.280
"Then, of course! Some soap!"

00:07:28.340 --> 00:07:33.193
He runs down the table leg and across the floor.

00:07:33.252 --> 00:07:36.566
Zaza's bathroom door is open.

00:07:36.626 --> 00:07:40.158
Marcel goes in and looks up.

00:07:40.218 --> 00:07:43.640
A soap dish is above his head.

00:07:43.700 --> 00:07:47.672
Ten seconds later, he's sitting in it.

00:07:47.732 --> 00:07:50.834
He puts some soap on his neck.

00:07:50.894 --> 00:07:56.056
Then he closes his eyes and pulls again.

00:07:56.116 --> 00:07:58.238
Yes!

00:07:58.298 --> 00:08:02.180
This time the diamond ring comes off.

00:08:02.239 --> 00:08:06.532
In the morning, Zaza finds the White Star.

00:08:06.592 --> 00:08:11.704
It's on her bedroom table between two perfume bottles.

00:08:11.764 --> 00:08:15.327
"But I don't understand,"

00:08:15.347 --> 00:08:21.404
she says. "Thieves don't bring things back."

00:08:21.464 --> 00:08:24.791
She looks at the ring.

00:08:24.851 --> 00:08:28.472
Then she looks at her face in the mirror.

00:08:28.532 --> 00:08:31.633
Then she looks at the ring again.

00:08:31.694 --> 00:08:35.144
"And why is there soap on it?"

00:08:35.205 --> 00:08:38.436
She telephones the police.

00:08:38.496 --> 00:08:43.658
Next day, Zaza's story is in all the newspapers.

00:08:43.718 --> 00:08:49.668
"Opera star's one-million-pound ring is safe," says one.

00:08:49.728 --> 00:08:54.638
"Thieves bring back Dupont diamond," says another.

00:08:54.698 --> 00:08:57.911
"Now police ask why."

00:08:57.971 --> 00:09:02.954
And there are lots of photos of Zaza with the White Star.

00:09:03.014 --> 00:09:09.630
At home, at the Opera House, standing in front of the Eiffel Tower.

00:09:09.690 --> 00:09:13.152
She looks very happy in all of them.

00:09:13.212 --> 00:09:15.835
Marcel's happy too.

00:09:15.895 --> 00:09:20.300
Back on his boat, he reads the newspaper stories.

00:09:20.360 --> 00:09:22.984
Then he looks in the mirror.

00:09:23.044 --> 00:09:27.065
There's a thin red line on his neck.

00:09:27.125 --> 00:09:32.356
"Oh, what a night!" he says.

00:09:32.416 --> 00:09:38.628
After that he washes, has breakfast and opens the window.

00:09:38.688 --> 00:09:42.180
It's a beautiful warm morning.

00:09:42.240 --> 00:09:47.601
Marcel looks up at the blue sky and smiles.

00:09:47.661 --> 00:09:53.468
"Now," he thinks, "what's going to happen today?"
